Z||000007||wkayl||06-28-2000||04:43 PM||||Yea I wish for the old days again like when I picked up a 67 GTO with 60,000 miles for $300 or the 70 AAR Cuda I got for a 70 Toyota and $200, or the 71 Challenger R/T I traded the GTO for, or the 67 Mustang coupe with the 390ci. A/C, P/S tilt away steering I passed up because the wanted way too much money ($275). Or when I went into the full service gas station  with my 67 Impala 2 door and the guy was shocked because he had never ben able to put $11 in gas in a car befor.  But then again when I had those cars it was just after I got my big raise to $2.75/hr.  If you figure it out, with todays dollars, my 86 Fiero G/T cost me less than those cars.||||reg||1
